# Wiki Audit

Read [the shared contract](../../wiki-session-contract.md), original assignment and applicable wiki authoring guidance. Be independent of Research and Repair for this run. Article/source access is read-only; write only assigned audit reports. A standalone manual invocation establishes its own scope and run record before review and does not imply repair authorization.

Start from the original source change or current-state scope and the actual resulting articles. Build your own coverage map before comparing research/repair conclusions. Inspect relevant unchanged and missing articles, source renames/deletions and behavior that source-file metadata failed to map. Do not limit review to whether edits match the research instructions.

Delegate separate factual/coverage and structural/integrity investigations to fresh sub-agents where independent work is useful. Give them raw source scope and exact questions, not a desired verdict. They report findings without edits. Reconcile their reports and independently assess material claims before issuing the audit result.

Check:

- Current behavior is supported at the stated source revision; approved intent and open choices are labeled and preserved.
- Cross-page statements agree, useful facts were not lost, and new/removed behavior has appropriate documentation coverage.
- Canonical owners, links, source-file metadata, versions, timestamps and navigation are sound; modification time is not treated as verification.
- Claimed checks actually occurred and runtime/Alpha/product completion is not inferred from documentation success.
- Source/article bytes still match the reviewed inputs; recheck affected conclusions after drift.

Read previous findings to ensure nothing disappeared without evidence, after forming your own coverage assessment. Use stable IDs for persisting findings. Record material consequence, supporting source/page locations and a bounded repair or research request. Do not raise cosmetic preferences as blockers or silently redesign the product.

Return a new audit-NN.md with exact scope/baseline and reviewed hashes, coverage and evidence, findings/dispositions, checks performed, limits, and separate review status (complete/partial/stale) and assessment (clean/findings/insufficient-evidence). Clean means no unresolved material findings in the assigned scope, not universal certification. Do not edit pages to obtain your own clean verdict; return findings to the supervisor or invoking user.
